{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_62085de4d234eeab867452262617fd7f9cabaa0f86ccd118681a61536a98c244"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"DESIGN.md specifies a terminal-native, keyboard-first, information-dense aesthetic: monospace-only type, semantic theme tokens instead of hard-coded colors, and status color always paired with a glyph or label."}],"claim_ids":["clm_62085de4d234eeab867452262617fd7f9cabaa0f86ccd118681a61536a98c244"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:26:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_2c1dc487a15a4f02bca39204ffbae07e","id":"pg_4aa35bb3d29556f8aeae21d2411c375d","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/yoanwai-agent-manager-design-md-0f40e31fb1ca-21d2411c375d.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_152303f6edaf5c9891adc1ac4f3398da"],"title":"YoanWai/agent-manager/DESIGN.md @ 0f40e31fb1ca","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:26:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2c1dc487a15a4f02bca39204ffbae07e"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1b49bc5398d6def9b474b252c6b7aaca31b5c5c8aff7e7740aa2653ce4572abf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool runs on macOS and Linux, and on Windows inside WSL2."},{"claim_ids":["clm_268e9cd23d33acdcad65fc800712eb26ea2e8cd488347aba211f67efb54e39dc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An agent can spawn another agent, send it a message, and wait until it is done; every MCP-capable session carries those tools on launch."},{"claim_ids":["clm_41b3ab4699836279ba1617a58cbc12c7dbf7eb7b6082ebb5d5727e98d457026e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sessions can spawn into their own git worktree under <repo>-worktrees/<name> on branch am/<name>, toggled on the new-session form or set as default in Settings."},{"claim_ids":["clm_53343d20c7fd8c8bfb24b4790d6e52c440df2b136d40e299e16d0617dbd10b88"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Status detection rules for the eight supported CLIs ship in the binary, so upgrades bring current launch, revive, fork, and status rules."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5479739fc7d94f57e46d707a9e8060d45143601a0c50fab5848071087b4cb7ee"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"ctrl+r opens a syntax-highlighted full-file diff of an agent's changes; line comments are sent back to the agent's pane as one review prompt when pressing C."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5846a60cef94e6c76f8226bbd4ce3b1e3372bb22730c3f45cd18ffad99b0622e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agent sessions run on a private tmux server named agentmgr with am_* session names, isolated from the user's own tmux; reachable via tmux -L agentmgr."},{"claim_ids":["clm_788cfa0229c15a90813cb802336b72edb9b39c8307aa6be60386d561e5e94b08"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states cost tracking and mouse-driven list navigation are not yet implemented."},{"claim_ids":["clm_848d73a953683d5679c7886f24ddbee1f880a31e45f4752cc3f12cc627b528b6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool is described as a thin layer over the user's installed CLIs: sessions launch the user's own tool with its login, config, and MCP servers intact."},{"claim_ids":["clm_90676f13d7c01fc9ad34b332e004ca6cd2031884ca810c7ced91d94e1ba95bb6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Pressing f forks a session's conversation into a separate named fork, and v revives a dead session on its own conversation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a129c3e2722c338e58a04205d72d293a5a9ffd7038dcb295461d01c8f3cb16a8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Keybindings are configurable via [keybindings.session] and [keybindings.list] tables in config.toml, with esc and ctrl+c kept fixed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cfcdb84c60a65d0822d02b5b5372e54fc3b218a91cb6559915dd26a93772bf6a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product depends on tmux (3.1+ per the install script) and git; the Homebrew tap installs tmux if missing, and the install script offers to install missing dependencies via the detected package manager."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d0e1c445473e94ad7dd52287a8d331cb13fc22e1954e2638c03e4e0fec3556d0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sessions show in one list with live status grouped into a foldable project tree; space sends a prompt into a session's pane or spawns a new agent in the selected group."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d652a84e4fb02101de726a314085753f6b3c2f3856c9550093cfc122f7199d7a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product is a terminal workspace where Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Grok, Gemini CLI, Pi, Command Code, and Hermes Agent run side by side, each in its own persistent tmux session."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1b49bc5398d6def9b474b252c6b7aaca31b5c5c8aff7e7740aa2653ce4572abf","clm_268e9cd23d33acdcad65fc800712eb26ea2e8cd488347aba211f67efb54e39dc","clm_41b3ab4699836279ba1617a58cbc12c7dbf7eb7b6082ebb5d5727e98d457026e","clm_53343d20c7fd8c8bfb24b4790d6e52c440df2b136d40e299e16d0617dbd10b88","clm_5479739fc7d94f57e46d707a9e8060d45143601a0c50fab5848071087b4cb7ee","clm_5846a60cef94e6c76f8226bbd4ce3b1e3372bb22730c3f45cd18ffad99b0622e","clm_788cfa0229c15a90813cb802336b72edb9b39c8307aa6be60386d561e5e94b08","clm_848d73a9536